Commercial use does not require a separate licensing fee
or additional permission under the MIT License.

### 3.2 Modification

Users may modify, extend, optimize, refactor, or otherwise
adapt the software to meet their technical requirements.

Modified versions may be distributed under different
licensing terms, provided the original MIT copyright and
permission notices are retained as required.

### 3.3 Distribution

Users may distribute original or modified copies of EveryO
through public repositories, private repositories, software
packages, or other distribution channels.

The applicable copyright and license notices must be
included in copies or substantial portions of the software.

### 3.4 Private Use

EveryO may be used, studied, modified, and deployed
privately without an obligation under the MIT License
to publish modifications or disclose proprietary source code.

### 3.5 Sublicensing

The MIT License permits sublicensing, subject to preserving
the required original copyright and permission notices.

### 3.6 Integration

EveryO may be integrated into applications, libraries,
machine learning pipelines, research tools, and other
software systems.

The MIT License does not require the entire integrating
application to be distributed under the MIT License.

